# Hang Loyalty integration

This project integrates with **Hang Loyalty** — the source of truth for points
and rewards. When working on loyalty features, follow the bundled
`hang-loyalty-integration` skill and verify against the sandbox with the
`hang-loyalty` MCP server.

Non-negotiables:

- All Hang calls are **server-side**. `HANG_API_KEY` is a secret — never expose
  it to client code.
- Configure via env vars: `HANG_API_BASE_URL`, `HANG_API_KEY`,
  `HANG_ACTIVITY_TYPE_ID`.
- One membership per user, keyed by your stable `external_user_id`; persist the
  returned membership id.
- Always pass an `idempotency_key` (your order id) when reporting activities.
- Display and gate redemptions with `spendable_balance`, not `balance`.
- One earning rail per order type: partner API for app orders, Toast for
  in-store — never report Toast orders as activities (double-earns).
- The MCP server is a dev-time verification tool; production code calls the
  partner API directly over HTTP.
